.TH "pipx" "1" "" "" "User Commands"
.SH Name
pipx \- install and run Python applications in isolated environments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.sp
\fBpipx\fP [\fIglobal\-options\fP] [\fBinstall\fP | \fBinstall\-all\fP | \fBuninject\fP | \fBinject\fP | \fBexpose\fP | \fBunexpose\fP |
\fBpin\fP | \fBunpin\fP | \fBupgrade\fP | \fBupgrade\-all\fP | \fBupgrade\-shared\fP | \fBuninstall\fP | \fBuninstall\-all\fP | \fBreset\fP
| \fBreinstall\fP | \fBreinstall\-all\fP | \fBhealth\fP | \fBrepair\fP | \fBlist\fP | \fBinterpreter\fP | \fBcache\fP | \fBmanifest\fP |
\fBrun\fP | \fBexec\fP | \fBrunpip\fP | \fBensurepath\fP | \fBenvironment\fP | \fBcompletions\fP | \fBhelp\fP] [\fIcommand\-options\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.sp
pipx installs and runs Python applications in isolated environments while exposing their commands on your
\fBPATH\fP\&.
.SH COMMANDS
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \fBinstall\fP
Install a package
.TP
.B \fBinstall\-all\fP
Install all packages
.TP
.B \fBuninject\fP
Uninstall injected packages from an existing Virtual Environment
.TP
.B \fBinject\fP
Install packages into an existing Virtual Environment
.TP
.B \fBexpose\fP
Restore resources from a hidden environment
.TP
.B \fBunexpose\fP
Hide resources without removing an environment
.TP
.B \fBpin\fP
Pin the specified package to prevent it from being upgraded
.TP
.B \fBunpin\fP
Unpin the specified package
.TP
.B \fBupgrade\fP
Upgrade a package
.TP
.B \fBupgrade\-all\fP
Upgrade all packages. Runs \fBpip install \-U <pkgname>\fP for each package.
.TP
.B \fBupgrade\-shared\fP
Upgrade shared libraries.
.TP
.B \fBuninstall\fP
Uninstall a package
.TP
.B \fBuninstall\-all\fP
Uninstall all packages
.TP
.B \fBreset\fP
Return pipx to a fresh install
.TP
.B \fBreinstall\fP
Reinstall a package
.TP
.B \fBreinstall\-all\fP
Reinstall all packages
.TP
.B \fBhealth\fP
Check installed package environments
.TP
.B \fBrepair\fP
Repair broken package environments
.TP
.B \fBlist\fP
List installed packages
.TP
.B \fBinterpreter\fP
Interact with interpreters managed by pipx
.TP
.B \fBcache\fP
Manage cached run environments
.TP
.B \fBmanifest\fP
Manage tools declared in an explicit manifest
.TP
.B \fBrun\fP
Download the latest version of a package to a temporary virtual environment, then run an app from it. Also
compatible with local \fB__pypackages__\fP directory (experimental).
.TP
.B \fBexec\fP
Run an application from an existing pipx environment
.TP
.B \fBrunpip\fP
Run pip in an existing pipx\-managed Virtual Environment
.TP
.B \fBensurepath\fP
Ensure directories necessary for pipx operation are in your PATH environment variable.
.TP
.B \fBenvironment\fP
Print a list of environment variables and paths used by pipx.
.TP
.B \fBcompletions\fP
Print instructions on enabling shell completions for pipx
.TP
.B \fBhelp\fP
Show help for pipx or a command
.UNINDENT
.sp
Run \fBpipx\fP \fIcommand\fP \fB\-\-help\fP for command\-specific options.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \fB\-h\fP, \fB\-\-help\fP
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B \fB\-\-version\fP
Print version and exit
.UNINDENT
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \fBPIPX_HOME\fP
Directory for pipx\-managed environments and state.
.TP
.B \fBPIPX_BIN_DIR\fP
Directory where pipx exposes application commands.
.TP
.B \fBPIPX_DEFAULT_PYTHON\fP
Default interpreter used to create environments.
.TP
.B \fBPIPX_USE_EMOJI\fP
Set to \fB0\fP to disable emoji output.
.UNINDENT
.SH SEE ALSO
.sp
Full documentation: \%<https://\:pipx\:.pypa\:.io/>
.sp
\fBpip\fP(1), \fBvirtualenv\fP(1)
.SH AUTHORS
.sp
Chad Smith and contributors
.sp
